  "raw_text": "Step 1: To find \\( f^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right) \\), we need to determine the value of \\( x \\) such that \\( f(x) = \\frac{1}{5} \\).\n\nStep 2: Set up the equation based on the function definition: \\[ \\frac{2}{x+1} = \\frac{1}{5} \\]\n\nStep 3: Solve for \\( x \\). Start by cross-multiplying to eliminate the fractions: \\[ 2 \\cdot 5 = 1 \\cdot (x + 1) \\]\n\\[ 10 = x + 1 \\]\n\nStep 4: Isolate \\( x \\): \\[ x = 10 - 1 \\]\n\\[ x = 9 \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{9}<|im_end|>",
